## Routes B and C: ask for text instead

Then I tried the obvious thing I should have started with. `agy` can run with `--json-schema` for structured output and no tools, so I asked for text:

- **Route B, sprite rows.** A JSON array of strings, one per row, one character per pixel, plus a palette mapping each character to a colour. For a 14×14 checkbox it got the size and palette exactly right on the first try
- **Route C, drawing code.** JavaScript against Scriptoscope's tiny Raster API (set a pixel, fill a rect, and so on). It drew a correct slider thumb on the first try

