## The best result: claude-pxl

[claude-pxl](https://github.com/crsolver/claude-pxl) (MIT) is an Agent Skill for "pixel art as code". The model writes a `.px.js` file containing a palette and text grids or shape operations, and the skill builds PNGs, enlarged previews and an ASCII dump you can check by eye. It is route B with proper tooling around it.

What I liked:

- The PNGs come out at exactly the size in the file, with alpha strictly 0 or 255, which is what a 1-bit mask needs
- A build takes about 0.1 seconds
- It has no dependencies beyond Node

It is packaged as a Claude skill, but its docs work fine as plain context for another model. I gave `agy` claude-pxl's own `SKILL.md` and reference docs as context, and Gemini wrote all eight Halcyon control sprites in one go. Every one of them round-tripped exactly through Scriptoscope's encoder and the runtime decoder.

